+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool calls are untrusted provider output, so the registry validates them at the single boundary before an executor can act on them.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the resolved definition's JSON Schema before it invokes the executor. A rejected call returns a `ToolResponse` that identifies the failing property and constraint for `required`, declared type, and `enum` violations, without exposing an input value in that result or its logs; an input that validates, including an unlisted property, reaches the executor unchanged ([validated by: returns redacted required, type, and enum failures before an executor receives malformed input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L31)).
+
+- An unknown tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`. Static schemas compile when registered, so an invalid schema throws then and names its tool; a schema returned by a definition source is resolved and validated for each call rather than against a stale prior definition ([validated by: passes schema-valid unknown properties through unchanged while retaining unknown-tool errors and compiling static schemas only at registration](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L64)) ([validated by: uses the current function-supplied schema for every call instead of a stale schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L130)).
+
+## Tool loop
+
+A schema rejection is a tool result rather than an exception, allowing the provider to see the correction and retry within the existing tool-round budget ([validated by: returns a rejected call to the provider so it can retry with a corrected tool request](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
